```mdx
1. Run the frontend Jest suite including `Multi.test.tsx` at
`superset-frontend/plugins/legacy-preset-chart-deckgl/src/Multi/Multi.test.tsx`.

2. During `test('includes parent_slice_id in child slice requests when parent has
slice_id', ...)` starting at line 609, `DeckMulti` calls `SupersetClient.get({ endpoint:
url })` as implemented in `Multi.tsx:297-300`, where `url` already encodes `form_data` in
the query string via `getExploreLongUrl`.

3. The mocked client `mockGet` (set at `Multi.test.tsx:611-624`) receives calls where
`call[0]` only has an `endpoint` property; there is no `body` field passed to
`SupersetClient.get`, so `call[0].body` is `undefined`.

4. The test then executes `JSON.parse(call[0].body)` at `Multi.test.tsx:648`, `697`, and
`740`, which throws a runtime error (`JSON.parse` on `undefined`), causing all three
parent_slice_id tests to error out and never actually assert on the outgoing `form_data`
encoded in the URL.
