### Missing documentation for simplified first/last logic <sub>![category Documentation](https://img.shields.io/badge/Documentation-7c3aed)</sub>

<details>
  <summary>Tell me more</summary>

###### What is the issue?
The behavior of 'first' and 'last' modes is unclear as the previous sorter-based logic was removed without updating the documentation to explain the new simplified logic.

###### Why this matters
Developers maintaining this code won't understand why the sorting condition was removed and how the current implementation achieves the same result.

###### Suggested change ∙ *Feature Preview*
Add a comment explaining why the simple assignment logic is sufficient for first/last modes:
```javascript
// Simple assignment is sufficient since records are processed in order:
// 'first' keeps the first value, 'last' keeps the latest value seen
else if (mode === 'first') {
  this.val = this.val === null ? x : this.val;
} else if (mode === 'last') {
  this.val = x;
}
```


