**Suggestion:** When a search term is active, clicking a folder's collapse/expand control updates `collapsedIds` but has no effect on which items are actually collapsed, because `collapsedFolderIds` ignores `collapsedIds` during search and relies only on `searchExpandedFolderIds`; this leads to inconsistent UI (icon changes while children remain visible) and makes collapsing folders during search impossible. The fix is to factor in the difference between the pre-search collapse state and the current `collapsedIds` so that user-initiated collapses during search take effect while still auto-expanding folders when the search starts and restoring the original state when search is cleared. [logic error]

