body:
When checking `toCellBar`, consider automatically unchecking `toTextColor` and `toAllRow` to enforce mutual exclusivity at the state level, not just at the UI level through the `disabled` prop. Currently, if a user has `toTextColor` checked and then checks `toCellBar`, both flags could be true when the form is submitted.

Add state synchronization:
```typescript
onChange={event => {
  const checked = event.target.checked;
  setToCellBar(checked);
  if (checked) {
    setToTextColor(false);
    setToAllRow(false);
  }
}}
```

Similarly, when checking `toTextColor` or `toAllRow`, they should uncheck `toCellBar`.

