<summary><b>Steps of Reproduction ✅ </b></summary>

```mdx
1. Open `/user_info/` route (registered at `superset-frontend/src/views/routes.tsx:25` in
the shown snippet, path `/user_info/`), which lazy-loads `src/pages/UserInfo` and renders
`ApiKeyList` when `FeatureFlag.FabApiKeyEnabled` is true
(`superset-frontend/src/pages/UserInfo/index.tsx:216-221`).

2. On mount, `ApiKeyList` immediately starts request A via `useEffect -> fetchApiKeys()`
(`ApiKeyList.tsx:66-68`, request at `55-57`).

3. Before request A finishes (slow network), create a key from the same view: click
"Create API Key" (`ApiKeyList.tsx:199-201`), submit modal (`ApiKeyCreateModal.tsx:52-57`),
then close modal; this triggers `onSuccess()` (`ApiKeyCreateModal.tsx:78-81`) which calls
`fetchApiKeys()` again as request B (`ApiKeyList.tsx:216-218`).

4. If request B returns first, list is updated; if slower request A returns afterward,
`setApiKeys(...)` (`ApiKeyList.tsx:58`) overwrites newer data with stale results, and each
request independently runs `setLoading(false)` (`ApiKeyList.tsx:62`), so spinner can clear
while another fetch is still in flight.
