The comment states that the aria-label attribute 'should be available even if not rendered,' but virtual list items that are not rendered typically do not exist in the DOM at all. This comment may be misleading. Consider clarifying that the test waits for the option to be rendered when scrolled into view, or adjust the test approach if the option is not guaranteed to be in the DOM.
```suggestion
  // Virtual list only renders visible items, so we wait for the option to be rendered
  // and then search the DOM for the option element by its aria-label attribute
