### Overly broad WHERE clause removal in totals query <sub>![category Functionality](https://img.shields.io/badge/Functionality-0284c7)</sub>

<details>
  <summary>Tell me more</summary>

###### What is the issue?
The code removes the entire WHERE clause from totals query, but this removes ALL WHERE conditions, not just AG Grid filters. This could include legitimate WHERE conditions that should be preserved in totals calculations.


###### Why this matters
This will cause totals to be calculated incorrectly when there are non-AG Grid WHERE conditions (like time range filters, dashboard filters, etc.) that should still apply to the totals subquery.

###### Suggested change ∙ *Feature Preview*
Instead of deleting the entire WHERE clause, selectively remove only AG Grid-related WHERE conditions while preserving other legitimate WHERE conditions:

```typescript
const totalsExtras = { ...extras };
// Only remove AG Grid WHERE clause if it exists, preserve other WHERE conditions
if (ownState.agGridComplexWhere && totalsExtras.where === ownState.agGridComplexWhere) {
  delete totalsExtras.where;
} else if (ownState.agGridComplexWhere && totalsExtras.where?.includes(ownState.agGridComplexWhere)) {
  // If AG Grid WHERE is part of a larger WHERE clause, remove just that part
  totalsExtras.where = totalsExtras.where.replace(ownState.agGridComplexWhere, '').replace(/^\s*AND\s*|\s*AND\s*$/, '').trim();
}
```


