### Missing useEffect dependencies <sub>![category Functionality](https://img.shields.io/badge/Functionality-0284c7)</sub>

<details>
  <summary>Tell me more</summary>

###### What is the issue?
The useEffect has missing dependencies in its dependency array, specifically `isFilterVisible`, `lastFilteredInputPosition`, and `handleFilterClick`.


###### Why this matters
This can cause stale closures where the effect uses outdated values of these variables, leading to incorrect behavior or infinite re-renders when these values change.

###### Suggested change ∙ *Feature Preview*
Add all referenced variables to the dependency array:

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  setTimeout(() => {
    if (lastFilteredColumn === colId && !isFilterVisible) {
      handleFilterClick();
      focusFilterInput(lastFilteredInputPosition);
    }
  }, 200);
}, [lastFilteredColumn, colId, isFilterVisible, lastFilteredInputPosition, handleFilterClick, focusFilterInput]);
```

