### Missing setTimeout cleanup <sub>![category Functionality](https://img.shields.io/badge/Functionality-0284c7)</sub>

<details>
  <summary>Tell me more</summary>

###### What is the issue?
The setTimeout in useEffect is not cleaned up, which can cause memory leaks and race conditions if the component unmounts before the timeout executes.


###### Why this matters
If the component unmounts or the effect re-runs before the 200ms timeout completes, the callback will still execute with potentially stale references, leading to errors or unwanted side effects.

###### Suggested change ∙ *Feature Preview*
Return a cleanup function from the useEffect:

```typescript
useEffect(() => {
  const timeoutId = setTimeout(() => {
    if (lastFilteredColumn === colId && !isFilterVisible) {
      handleFilterClick();
      focusFilterInput(lastFilteredInputPosition);
    }
  }, 200);

  return () => clearTimeout(timeoutId);
}, [lastFilteredColumn, colId, isFilterVisible, lastFilteredInputPosition, handleFilterClick, focusFilterInput]);
```


